{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it","id":490214,"title":"Build yourown Mockery breed, because I'm a Mage damn it!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-23T22:31:34-07:00","id":490214,"title":"Build yourown Mockery breed, because I'm a Mage damn it!","content":"So in the Werewolf20 line the book of the wyrm introduces Mockery Breeds, artificial wyrm changing breeds built in various pentex labs. I am assuming with enough spheres and a proper celestial patron a mage might be able to replicate this feat(and why? because Science! that's why!) I am thinking spirit 5, Life 5, Prime 5 as the prereques on spheres but am open to other options. Anyone have any thoughts going forward? I imagine at least one &quot;the wyrm tricks you into making a new tool&quot; will come up and its a cool angle for a plot but other options might be interesting, available patrons, why they'd want things etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T23:17:04-07:00","id":490252,"title":"","content":"Using Mage: the Ascension rules to build your own Mockery Breed in order to facilitate crossovers with Werewolf: the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Sir, I think you have entirely too much time on your hands.<br /> <br /> And I applaud you for it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T00:47:10-07:00","id":490290,"title":"","content":"Sure, why not? sounds superfun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Only problem it's that damn pesky Paradox, always interfering with our Science! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But what if we managed some sort of bargain with a Bane, or something on these lines, that worked similar than the pact with a Familiar. To allow our cute horror to survive Paradox a bit longer while in &quot;wolf-beast form&quot;, by absorbing and nulling it (to an extent).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T03:49:13-07:00","id":490379,"title":"","content":"Let's see, I'm sure we can improve on some of the existing Changing Breeds, while we're at it, so let's begin with the Baset:<br /> <br /> -Existing, we'll want Life 5 and Prime 5.<br /> -Shape shifting: Life 5, use the spell 1-4 times depending on how many forms we want it to have.<br /> -Spiritual stuff: a lot of really weird things, but basically Spirit 5.<br /> -Breeding: Life 'we don't care we already made life' once to make it breed true with humans, another for the correct animal, and a third for others of it's mockery breed.<br /> -Any additional powers we want!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T06:23:52-07:00","id":490461,"title":"","content":"There's only one group that could create a Mockery Breed race, the Technocracy. They have the infrastructure to do so. Others can create such creatures but they'd be hard pressed to create them in real numbers. And the Progenitors have created artificial life already, from clones to the genegineered creatures.<br /> <br /> They could create a Mockery Breed of their own, they have the means and the know-how. The problem is that Dimensional Science (Spirit) is largely the domain of the Void Engineers. Yes there are those outside the Convention but there are few DimSci masters outside of the VE. So they would probably lacking when in comes to the Spirit side of things. However that can be made up with various cybernetics and biomods that can simulate all kinds of powers.<br /> <br /> And of course its unlikely the Garou would see it as Wyrm-tainted, something made by the Technocracy would more likely be seen as Weaver-tainted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T06:32:41-07:00","id":490465,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">This sounds like a good excuse to mess with the Special Projects/Syndicate ties inside Pentex. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T06:36:32-07:00","id":490466,"title":"","content":"Mind 5, Spirit 5. Mind to dull the hosts will and Spirit to do the binding. Once the spirit has taken over the host, just keep using Spirit to guide the spirit to manifest its nature physically. Shapeshifting won't be to hard for the spirit to figure out, maybe a couple of unique powers to the new mockery, but gifts would be completely out of the question without a powerful spirit to act as a sponsor in the spirit world.<br /> <br /> The Mage obviously would have to have a strong understanding of how Spirit Possession and Spirit Pacts work, but this is how I would do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T09:49:15-07:00","id":490643,"title":"","content":"Are you looking to just get critters who can shift between 3 or 5 forms (or just 2)? Or do you want the whole slew of spirit related stuff that the Changing Breeds tack on? <br /> <br /> The first project seems pretty easy. It may require some high levels of Life and several stacked effects. <br /> <br /> Adding on the ersatz-shaman-like stuff is a whole 'nuther ball of wax. That would be HUGE. And it's going to be something the Union will HIGHLY disapprove of, for obvious reasons. Some of the various nonsensical powers might be duplicate-able in terms of &quot;real science&quot; (which is neither actually real, nor actually science).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T11:35:35-07:00","id":490754,"title":"","content":"The spiritual aspect of things really doesn't seem to be in the Technocracy's wheelhouse. You might get a really dedicated Nephandus with enough clout among evil spirits to pull something like this off, but my impression is that the capable ones are off doing their own thing and not working with Pentex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T13:08:11-07:00","id":490853,"title":"","content":"An independant (and likely mad) Archmage also could have the necessary power/resources/know-how to create such beasties. And a Realm/really big Sanctum to put them all. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T21:42:12-07:00","id":491275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=490461#post490461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's only one group that could create a Mockery Breed race, the Technocracy. They have the infrastructure to do so. Others can create such creatures but they'd be hard pressed to create them in real numbers. And the Progenitors have created artificial life already, from clones to the genegineered creatures.<br /> <br /> They could create a Mockery Breed of their own, they have the means and the know-how. The problem is that Dimensional Science (Spirit) is largely the domain of the Void Engineers. Yes there are those outside the Convention but there are few DimSci masters outside of the VE. So they would probably lacking when in comes to the Spirit side of things. However that can be made up with various cybernetics and biomods that can simulate all kinds of powers.<br /> <br /> And of course its unlikely the Garou would see it as Wyrm-tainted, something made by the Technocracy would more likely be seen as Weaver-tainted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They would also need the proper sort of patron on part with Gaia or the wyrm. Well I've already done one crossover logic here lets take another jump. The Patron they have on par would be Autochthon, who would be masquerading as the Computer for IX. Of course his creatures would be bit more mechanical, so a human who turns into a robot or a robot that turns into a human. Come to think of it IX has something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T07:59:51-07:00","id":491656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=490754#post490754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spiritual aspect of things really doesn't seem to be in the Technocracy's wheelhouse. You might get a really dedicated Nephandus with enough clout among evil spirits to pull something like this off, but my impression is that the capable ones are off doing their own thing and not working with Pentex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I was extending the idea to making &quot;Mockeries&quot; that were just manufactured shapeshifters that didn't have the Changing Breed baggage. Like, say, if a Verbena wanted to &quot;reward&quot; (or curse) a person or bloodline. Or a Progenitor or SoE had &quot;gone Moreau&quot; with a twist of lime. But if you want your mock-Mockeries to come with all the Banes attached, you're going to need a Nephandus or Infernalist or a very very bad person like a Voormas of Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T22:36:39-07:00","id":492360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=491656#post491656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. I was extending the idea to making &quot;Mockeries&quot; that were just manufactured shapeshifters that didn't have the Changing Breed baggage. Like, say, if a Verbena wanted to &quot;reward&quot; (or curse) a person or bloodline. Or a Progenitor or SoE had &quot;gone Moreau&quot; with a twist of lime. But if you want your mock-Mockeries to come with all the Banes attached, you're going to need a Nephandus or Infernalist or a very very bad person like a Voormas of Life.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well its more a point of a theoretical mage running into a mockery finding out backstory and being &quot;Wait you can make them with science.. I do Science...&quot; and in an act of extreme hubris tries to recreate it. Now most likely this is going ot fail. Or get the wyrm in some fashion to abuse the hubris. But lets assume the mage is spiritually understanding enough to get around that and tries to find another source for her would be shapechanging supernatural breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T01:07:42-07:00","id":492415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=491656#post491656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. I was extending the idea to making &amp;quot;Mockeries&amp;quot; that were just manufactured shapeshifters that didn't have the Changing Breed baggage. Like, say, if a Verbena wanted to &amp;quot;reward&amp;quot; (or curse) a person or bloodline. Or a Progenitor or SoE had &amp;quot;gone Moreau&amp;quot; with a twist of lime. But if you want your mock-Mockeries to come with all the Banes attached, you're going to need a Nephandus or Infernalist or a very very bad person like a Voormas of Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Verbena or probably Dreamspeaker.<br /> <br /> Not Technocracy, not only because the union would not approve, but because that kind of creature would not fit any technocrat paradigm. It would be as impossible for them to create a new race of faeries, they just can't believe that's even possible.<br /> <br /> Speaking about systems, I remember the Werewolf Storyteller Handbook stating that it would be impossible for Mages even to use their magic to increase the probabilities of having Garou descendants from a Kinfolk couple, because it would be messing with cosmological rules blah blah blah. I found it quite absurd, but those corossover rulesets were more about avoiding player abuse than about a good or logical interaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3673-mu_","name":"Mu_","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3673_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T08:58:03-07:00","id":492616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=492360#post492360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well its more a point of a theoretical mage running into a mockery finding out backstory and being &quot;Wait you can make them with science.. I do Science...&quot; and in an act of extreme hubris tries to recreate it. Now most likely this is going ot fail. Or get the wyrm in some fashion to abuse the hubris. But lets assume the mage is spiritually understanding enough to get around that and tries to find another source for her would be shapechanging supernatural breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is that an act of extreme hubris? Or an act of hubris? Why would it involve the Wyrm? Just because the enemies of the Garou are so limited as to have to use that particular paradigm doesn't bind a mage to it. In fact, if it HAS to be a technomagic-based creation process, the mage in question might not have anything related to such an entity in their paradigm.<br /> <br /> &quot;Aha! I have made a human-baboon spectrum hybrid by splicing DNA of a <i>Mandrillus sphinx</i> as an accompanying intertwined helix with a hyper-phosphate bond de-re-coupler molecular interface! How did I overcome the intron incompatibility factors? I'm glad you asked! I was able to use the implicate harmonization of the composite subatomic superstrings to overcame the inherent discrepencies! Of course, such harmonization has resulted in several side-effects similar to those evinced in ultra-dimensional standing-resonant-pattern beings... But, overall, that has enhanced the outcome of the experiment! Wait, what do you mean that mandrills aren't actually baboons?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 04-26-2015, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T09:05:47-07:00","id":492622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mu_</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=492415#post492415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not Technocracy, not only because the union would not approve, but because that kind of creature would not fit any technocrat paradigm. It would be as impossible for them to create a new race of faeries, they just can't believe that's even possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that.... <br /> <br /> Why would the Union fetter the hands of the Progenitors so severely? I'm sure the splicing of animal DNA into baseline human genomes is definitely on the boards all over the place. There's just too much extant potential out there that might be used for a variety of effects: adaptation to extreme environments, enhancing abilities, creation of subservient species for various targeted purposes, etc. Such extreme experiments as those that would produce a Mockery analogue might be restricted to secure labs, but even if the final outcome might be kept in reserve for specific situational deployment (like biological versions of HIT-MARKS, perhaps even using them in anti-shifter capacities.... fighting fire with fire, as it were), the spin-off biotech might have amazingly diverse (and more subtle) applications....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T17:00:10-07:00","id":493015,"title":"","content":"Well I think the implication of Mockeries is skewing the discussion on this topic. It's not relevant whether or not they are Mockeries in the Werewolf sense. Let's just go beyond that and go with magic created shapeshifters. This is pretty much the Progenitors do. There is a number of hermetic spells that create homonculi and servants, and there are Golems for the Lions of Zion.<br /> <br /> So, let's ignore the Werewolf cosomology and ideas and just focus on how to make magical shapeshifters with Mage. Anything else is way too mucked up with crossover country.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T03:35:29-07:00","id":497288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=492622#post492622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know about that.... <br /> <br /> Why would the Union fetter the hands of the Progenitors so severely? I'm sure the splicing of animal DNA into baseline human genomes is definitely on the boards all over the place. There's just too much extant potential out there that might be used for a variety of effects: adaptation to extreme environments, enhancing abilities, creation of subservient species for various targeted purposes, etc. Such extreme experiments as those that would produce a Mockery analogue might be restricted to secure labs, but even if the final outcome might be kept in reserve for specific situational deployment (like biological versions of HIT-MARKS, perhaps even using them in anti-shifter capacities.... fighting fire with fire, as it were), the spin-off biotech might have amazingly diverse (and more subtle) applications....</div> </div> </div> </div>Technocracy has been fighting myths for a long time, it seems not very productive encouraging them.<br /> <br /> Supposing they want to, the main problem is the paradigm. I'm sorry for Asmodai, but I think that if they are WtA style shapeshifters isthe key of the question.<br /> <br /> WtA shapeshifting works through the fusion of matter and spirit. This is just something a Progenitor can't conceive. He can't do that.<br /> <br /> If a Progenitor want to develop a shapeshifter, he can not gain any insight studying werewikbes, since their fundamentals on changing are out of reach of his science.<br /> <br /> Suppose he wants to just imitate the capabilities by his own biological means. The feat would be very challenging, since there are many scientific objections to shape shifting (starting with mass conservation), but I think it could be done with a good number of successes and Paradox. OK, we have a shapeshifter, but he is not more similar to a true shapeshifter than a Mage using a spell, a Gangrel or a Pooka.<br /> <br /> Pentex can do the trick because they mix technology with spirit magic. I think that some Traditions that believe in spirits could come closer to WtA shapeshifters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3673-mu_","name":"Mu_","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3673_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T03:42:01-07:00","id":497290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=493015#post493015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I think the implication of Mockeries is skewing the discussion on this topic. It's not relevant whether or not they are Mockeries in the Werewolf sense. Let's just go beyond that and go with magic created shapeshifters. This is pretty much the Progenitors do. There is a number of hermetic spells that create homonculi and servants, and there are Golems for the Lions of Zion.<br /> <br /> So, let's ignore the Werewolf cosomology and ideas and just focus on how to make magical shapeshifters with Mage. Anything else is way too mucked up with crossover country.</div> </div> </div> </div>About the necessary magic, I think that life 5 to the shape shifting, Prime 4 to make it a permanent ability, and Spirit 5 to shape the spiritual essence. And a huge number of successes.<br /> <br /> The total number of successes could be reduced depending on how close the Mage can study a true shapeshifter, but I would require that at least he must gain knowledge speaking or studying an specimen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3673-mu_","user":"Mu_","date":". 04-30-2015, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3673-mu_","name":"Mu_","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3673_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:27:28-07:00","id":497655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mu_</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=497288#post497288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technocracy has been fighting myths for a long time, it seems not very productive encouraging them.<br /> <br /> Supposing they want to, the main problem is the paradigm. I'm sorry for Asmodai, but I think that if they are WtA style shapeshifters isthe key of the question.<br /> <br /> WtA shapeshifting works through the fusion of matter and spirit. This is just something a Progenitor can't conceive. He can't do that.<br /> <br /> If a Progenitor want to develop a shapeshifter, he can not gain any insight studying werewikbes, since their fundamentals on changing are out of reach of his science.<br /> <br /> Suppose he wants to just imitate the capabilities by his own biological means. The feat would be very challenging, since there are many scientific objections to shape shifting (starting with mass conservation), but I think it could be done with a good number of successes and Paradox. OK, we have a shapeshifter, but he is not more similar to a true shapeshifter than a Mage using a spell, a Gangrel or a Pooka.<br /> <br /> Pentex can do the trick because they mix technology with spirit magic. I think that some Traditions that believe in spirits could come closer to WtA shapeshifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>One really great way to de-fang magic is to show up with a technological version. It's a tactic they've tried very successfully before. They even do it to their own renegade siblings regularly. Co-opting belief and fitting into your paradigm reduces the amount of necessary prep info dissemination. Easier to show off a bio/cyber-techno-werewolf and have people &quot;get it&quot; then get the idea of transhumanist body/machine mind migration to sink in. <br /> <br /> But conservation of mass would be a must, so the werewolve-analogues would be big-uns and it would be easier to make them really sturdy short-faced bear looking wolves or something like a man-sized Crinos than trim them down. (Unless they have to shed or re-integrate biomass to change forms.... Which is delightfully repulsive.)<br /> <br /> And most likely nothing resembling Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T19:47:43-08:00","id":1499488,"title":"","content":"Wait, am i wrong in believing that the Technocracy had a hand in creating the existing Mockery Breeds. Sure they were created by Pentex, but in collaboration under the Special Projects Division. Which is a Multi-Convention Syndicate-Pentax collaboration that went rogue. So Yes a Technocracy Mage could indeed make a mockery breed because they already have. Sure it was with help from Pentex, but whats to stop a Progenitor from colaberating with Pentex to make it happen again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27686-magequill","name":"MageQuill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T01:28:52-08:00","id":1499505,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, I already did this a long time ago in my games. A rogue crazy techie designed the perfect ciborgs, Shapeshifters who turn into androids, the &quot;Metallians&quot;, and with his Spirit 5 even created a small spiritual court to teach them gifts.<br /> <br /> It is entirely doable for a powerful master to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T01:38:17-08:00","id":1499507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mu_</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=497288#post497288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technocracy has been fighting myths for a long time, it seems not very productive encouraging them.<br /> <br /> Supposing they want to, the main problem is the paradigm. I'm sorry for Asmodai, but I think that if they are WtA style shapeshifters isthe key of the question.<br /> <br /> WtA shapeshifting works through the fusion of matter and spirit. This is just something a Progenitor can't conceive. He can't do that.<br /> <br /> If a Progenitor want to develop a shapeshifter, he can not gain any insight studying werewikbes, since their fundamentals on changing are out of reach of his science.<br /> <br /> Suppose he wants to just imitate the capabilities by his own biological means. The feat would be very challenging, since there are many scientific objections to shape shifting (starting with mass conservation), but I think it could be done with a good number of successes and Paradox. OK, we have a shapeshifter, but he is not more similar to a true shapeshifter than a Mage using a spell, a Gangrel or a Pooka.<br /> <br /> Pentex can do the trick because they mix technology with spirit magic. I think that some Traditions that believe in spirits could come closer to WtA shapeshifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the complete opposite of what the Progenitors do. Do they create &quot;souless&quot; creatures? Yes. But they also create &quot;souled&quot; ones - ie, they use Dimensional Science 5 to create an &quot;anthropic field&quot; for their clones. Translation: they use Spirit to create souls.<br /> <br /> The Progenitors and Technocrats arent ignorant, and neither are they oblivious to the existance of the spirit world (use whatever technobabble applicable here).<br /> <br /> Progenitors are also well aware to the fact that Shapeshifting breeds are individuals &quot;infected&quot; with &quot;trans dimensional matter&quot;.<br /> <br /> Creating a Mockery Breed is well within the Paradigm of the Progenitors - in fact, so much so that I cant even see any reason why the hell they would NOT do it. The only reason I see for such programs to be shut down in my opinion is the classic &quot;containment breach&quot;, unleashing a new critter into the WoD (exactly like what happened in my games, and the Weaver has been might grateful of its new toy that the techies let loose in the world)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T04:55:41-08:00","id":1499639,"title":"","content":"Obviously going off piste by bringing up CTD, but Naming 5 could pull it off if the Kithain knew what a Mockery Breed was, and had access to spirits, animals and humans to Rewrite. Doing it without the spirits of the Middle Umbra taking note in the region and then telling on you to any Garou around... that's much harder. Basically there is a way to do it, but it'll wind up with you dead.<br /> <br /> As for doing it with Magick, you only need to make a handful, and then they can breed. However be careful! Mockery Breeds suck for a few reasons compared to 'true' changers, and here are two big hurdles you need to overcome as a result:<br /> <br /> - You need to create an Animal Kinfolk population. If the last Kinfolk Wolf were to die, then it would mean the current generation of Garou are the last. No Changing Breed can survive without animal kinfolk. Mockery Breeds seem to be an exception to this, but their artificial nature, and this lack of animal kinfolk, seems to have serious complications for them. A stable and safe population of animal kinfolk would help you to 'stabilize' your mockery breed. Say you were to convert 10% of Scottish Deer into Kinfolk to your new Weredeer - that would be a good start.<br /> <br /> - The spirit world will have no time or respect for them. Samsa barely scrape by learning Level 1 Gifts, and Level 1 only, because Cockroach is protecting them. He's a pretty powerful and respected Spirit, and that's all they have going. The Yeren have the full backing of one of the most senior members of Pentex outside of the Board (because he is one!) and they are Project Lycaon's biggest ever success, and yet they can never get above Rank 3. And why? Because the spirit world, even Wyrmish spirits, find them to be appalling artificial newcomers. They are only a few steps away from being as stable and workable as Corax, say, but they get no respect because they're new.<br /> <br /> So if you use Magick (or Cantrips/Unleashing) to make a Weredeer Mockery Breed, you'll want to do a big spiritual PR campaign for them, which might see some moderate returns within decades if you have Pentex or The Union or the entire Beast Courts or Garou Nation behind you. Genuine acceptance may take millenia, millenia the world doesn't have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T08:32:04-08:00","id":1499651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=490461#post490461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's only one group that could create a Mockery Breed race, the Technocracy. They have the infrastructure to do so. Others can create such creatures but they'd be hard pressed to create them in real numbers. And the Progenitors have created artificial life already, from clones to the genegineered creatures.<br /> <br /> They could create a Mockery Breed of their own, they have the means and the know-how. The problem is that Dimensional Science (Spirit) is largely the domain of the Void Engineers. Yes there are those outside the Convention but there are few DimSci masters outside of the VE. So they would probably lacking when in comes to the Spirit side of things. However that can be made up with various cybernetics and biomods that can simulate all kinds of powers.<br /> <br /> And of course its unlikely the Garou would see it as Wyrm-tainted, something made by the Technocracy would more likely be seen as Weaver-tainted.</div> </div> </div> </div>If SPD is still around in your version of the setting, and/or if they have a spiritual successor (no pun intended), they'd also be masters of Dimensional Science \u2014 and in fact would have mastered it in exactly the sorts of ways that would be needed for this sort of project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T10:02:49-08:00","id":1499658,"title":"","content":"To be honest, give Progenitors a big enough budget and a few years they will deliver you an entire Mockery Breed. Even if they for some reason decide against involving some Void Engineer specialist (why would they? They already have an answer in their paradigm and they can definitely replicate it. See the first quote.) they can replicate a vast majority of the abilities of a Fera even without it. Like Nanotech Integration for the hardiness and regen of a Werewolf, see the second quote. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technocracy Reloaded 182-183</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves and other transdimensional creatures exist in<br /> multiple states simultaneously, interacting with the physical<br /> Unit 5: Q Division 183<br /> world, as well as one or more dimensions adjacent. Thanks to<br /> this synergistic interaction, these Reality Deviants are capable of<br /> remarkable physical feats, such as shrugging off bullet wounds<br /> and throwing cars. The Pandimensional Anomaly Waveform<br /> Shutdown is an anchor. By flooding the subject\u2019s body with<br /> electrical shocks at a rotating frequency, the PAWS taser creates<br /> interference in the RD\u2019s transdimensional signal, disrupting<br /> the carrier waves connecting it to the dimensional threshold.<br /> The dual-manifested entity on the receiving end of this weapon<br /> loses the advantages their connection to other worlds provides.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Progenitors Revised 74</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nanotech integration is an advancement of an earlier<br /> effort between Iteration X and us. It\u2019s since evolved, becoming<br /> far more efficient. The recipient is loaded with nanobots<br /> that expel toxins from the body, regulate vital functions,<br /> destroy aberrant cells, and regenerate tissue at alarming<br /> rates. While massive and immediate trauma can still kill<br /> the host, nanotech integration offers remarkable effects that<br /> guarantee survival in all but the most extreme situations.<br /> The Procedure\u2019s recipient gains three dots of Stamina,<br /> and regenerates one health level every turn. Mundane<br /> drugs, diseases, and poisons will not affect her, even if<br /> desired (and has been used to detox a number of Void<br /> Engineer substance abusers). She does not age. The procedure<br /> requires massive resources. Currently, field scientists<br /> sign up for a waiting list that currently accommodates<br /> enough subjects to take at least two years. A character<br /> with Entropy, Life, or Matter 5 may destroy the nanobots<br /> without otherwise hurting the recipient. Otherwise, the<br /> nanobots are nigh impossible to remove without highly<br /> restricted access to Progenitor computer systems..</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T16:59:39-08:00","id":1499698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=1499658#post1499658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, give Progenitors a big enough budget and a few years they will deliver you an entire Mockery Breed. Even if they for some reason decide against involving some Void Engineer specialist (why would they? They already have an answer in their paradigm and they can definitely replicate it. See the first quote.) they can replicate a vast majority of the abilities of a Fera even without it. Like Nanotech Integration for the hardiness and regen of a Werewolf, see the second quote.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, aside from how easy it is to completely wipe out nanomachines. Garou don't suddenly lose their shapeshifter benefits from getting an MRI checkup done, after all. Though, one wonders how said nanomachines would fare if one of the Garou or Fera used a technology-disabling Gift. One ambush and some chaos gremlins later, and Senator Armstrong is brought back down to normal...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T00:32:47-08:00","id":1499726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=1499698#post1499698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, aside from how easy it is to completely wipe out nanomachines. Garou don't suddenly lose their shapeshifter benefits from getting an MRI checkup done, after all. Though, one wonders how said nanomachines would fare if one of the Garou or Fera used a technology-disabling Gift. One ambush and some chaos gremlins later, and Senator Armstrong is brought back down to normal...</div> </div> </div> </div>...why would it be easy to wipe out the nanomschines? Why would a normal MRI check even detect nanites? Why would even a Rank 2 Jam Technology Gift disable hypertech aka Willworking disgued as tech, especially something as advanced as this? <br /> <br /> Next thing you are going to tell me about how Hitmarks are easy targets (Which they aren't if you are wandering by the way, see the quote)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guide to the Technocracy 132</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We do not recommend allowing a player character to run a HIT Mark. The damned things are far too powerful, and the potential for abuse is far too great. (\u201cAnyone got a place for all these Get of Fenris pelts?\u201d)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T01:14:29-08:00","id":1499728,"title":"","content":"I think it likely that should the Technocracy do this, they might either<br /> A: recreate the Ratkin, because rats are the usual subject for experiments (and Ratkin are the best) <br /> B: recreate the extinct Bat Fera, because they're massive fans of Jared Leto's Morbius (or more seriously, because they're resistant to disease and flight is useful and mammals are less of a stretch than <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The technocracy should do it for no other reason than to prove they can do it. If they can do it, they can hypothesize all they want about entirely scientific ways the changing breeds could have come about. They can prove themselves superior to the Traditions who don't have such methods. Oh, sure, it has some useful applications like bettering someone's standard of living or improving their combat capability but.. yeah. The only real caveat is that they need to ensure that their new changing breed sticks to the correct, scientifically minded procedures when it comes to rites and such that they get involved in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T05:39:45-08:00","id":1499740,"title":"","content":"In my games, the Progenitors are the most scary of the conventions. They have a Hive-Mind species of &quot;Hunters&quot;, who are like a mix of the Xenomorphs from Alien and the Zerg Swarm from Starcraft / Insects from Starshiptroops. They use those abominations to hunt down other abominations across the Umbra. And they have the &quot;Metallians&quot;, a mockery breed of &quot;winged robots&quot;, who can turn their meat into metal (but eventually they escaped, and got &quot;captured&quot; by the Weaver, and now they are sort of a problem, long story. Their &quot;AI-like&quot; minds proved to be perfect for the Weaver, and they switched masters. Oh yes, and they now have full access to Gifts provided by the embodiment of Stasis, so they are much more powerful than when they were in the progenitors' labs. Luckly, there's only a few dozens of them... For now. But they can breed).<br /> <br /> Creating &quot;Mockery Breeds&quot; for the Progenitors wouldnt be just a matter of &quot;mad scientist&quot;, it would be a huge research effort to understand the Shapeshifters' condition... As for breeding powerful minions for their purposes. If those may get loose in the world is another story, security for those projects would be at the highest level - in the case of the Metallians, they heard the &quot;Weaver's Song&quot; immediatly after creation, so it was caused by an external unforseen contingency, which could not be predicted and was not expected. The Metallians were supposed to be programmable slaves, but this external force overrided all their mental protocols. Iteration X and Void Engineers still havent being able to determine what was the cause of this costly bug; in the meanwhile, the program has been shutdown permanently, obviously, and the creation of new &quot;trans dimensional entities&quot; put on hold for undetermined time. <br /> <br /> But again, this sort of project is exactly what the techies not only could do, but it's what they WOULD do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T08:15:26-08:00","id":1499754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=1499726#post1499726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...why would it be easy to wipe out the nanomschines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're extremely small devices that are subject to even tiny, widespread changes in larger forces?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would a normal MRI check even detect nanites? </div> </div> </div>Aside from Michael Chrichton's Prey, refer also visually to Terminator Genisys, when the T-3000 has to contend with this exact scenario, and T3: Rise of the Machines, where the T-X is similarly inconvenienced by a particle accelerator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would even a Rank 2 Jam Technology Gift disable hypertech aka Willworking disgued as tech, especially something as advanced as this? </div> </div> </div>Because it's technology. You don't get to have your cake and eat it too - if it's not technology reliant on known principles, it's not a part of the technocrat paradigm. Garou and Fera manipulating chaos gremlins from the Wyld to break down the physics that technology relies on is a direct challenge to the paradigm. Even knives can be disabled in this manner, so nanomachines probably aren't safe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Next thing you are going to tell me about how Hitmarks are easy targets (Which they aren't if you are wandering by the way, see the quote) </div> </div> </div>They are. The writers that thought otherwise were very bad at math. Four dice of countermagick at difficulty 8 comes out behind potentially double the dice pool at difficulty 4 (disabling complex electronics makes JT and Gremlins very easy to use). Jam Gun is similarly easy to use to take out their ranged weapons, and is Rank 1, so even more widespread; the CoGs have another variant that has a difficulty if WP (so, 5, for HIT Marks) and takes out all manufactured weapons for the admittedly not too long duration. War Drones empowered by the Weaver are substantially greater direct physical threat, because they can regenerate agg like Garou regenerate lethal, hit hard, and don't look even remotely different from any other human, as opposed to being 300 kg terminators that werebeasts, by dint of their senses, can instantly pick out of a crowd as wrong and dangerous without needing Sense Weaver (not commonly known, because everyone is concentrated on the Wyrm).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T10:09:15-08:00","id":1499762,"title":"","content":"I actually wrote a much better post but because it took so long it logged me out without me knowing and when I tried to post it I got &quot;Human Verification Error&quot;.<br /> I am so salty right now.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=1499754#post1499754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they're extremely small devices that are subject to even tiny, widespread changes in larger forces?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't speak nonsense, they are built so that their host survives all but the most horrendous amount of damage and they are built by Prime 5, Life 4, Matter 2. Why would such oxymoronic flaw would exists?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The recipient is loaded with nanobots<br /> that expel toxins from the body, regulate vital functions,<br /> destroy aberrant cells, and regenerate tissue at alarming<br /> rates. While massive and immediate trauma can still kill<br /> the host, nanotech integration offers remarkable effects that<br /> guarantee survival in all but the most extreme situations.<br /> The Procedure\u2019s recipient gains three dots of Stamina,<br /> and regenerates one health level every turn. Mundane<br /> drugs, diseases, and poisons will not affect her, even if<br /> desired (and has been used to detox a number of Void<br /> Engineer substance abusers). </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=1499754#post1499754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from Michael Chrichton's Prey, refer also visually to Terminator Genisys, when the T-3000 has to contend with this exact scenario, and T3: Rise of the Machines, where the T-X is similarly inconvenienced by a particle accelerator.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhuh, so give me an actual example of why please. If you want to bring other fictions facts about Nanites, I can do it too and we would go around giving contradictory examples.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=1499754#post1499754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's technology. You don't get to have your cake and eat it too - if it's not technology reliant on known principles, it's not a part of the technocrat paradigm. Garou and Fera manipulating chaos gremlins from the Wyld to break down the physics that technology relies on is a direct challenge to the paradigm. Even knives can be disabled in this manner, so nanomachines probably aren't safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you seen The Technocracy? Half the stuff they have aren't based on any known principles and the rest is outright technobabble that might as well be magic. Even at low levels, All Triggers Locked, to the highest, like Format Space.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All Triggers Locked (\u2022\u2022 Forces /<br /> \u2022\u2022 Matter)<br /> When you absolutely, positively must kill every motherfucker<br /> in the room, accept no substitutes. This wildly vulgar<br /> Procedure \u2014 a measure of last resort \u2014 allows a Black Suit or<br /> cyborg to snatch from a distance the guns of every person in<br /> the immediate vicinity, snap them back to the agent\u2019s hands,<br /> merge them all together into a single line of firearms, lock their<br /> triggers, and fire them all simultaneously until the guns run<br /> out of ammunition. There\u2019s no way to aim the resulting hail<br /> of bullets but so long as the agent doesn\u2019t care about collateral<br /> damage, there\u2019s not much chance of escaping the carnage, either. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Format Space<br /> (Correspondence \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf,<br /> Dimensional Science \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Void Engineers prefer to regulate extraterrestrial space the easy way: by creating safe models of its phenomena for ordinary citizens to absorb, internalize and impose on the target region. Human minds collapse a region\u2019s dangerous possibilities into manageable Conventional Space. But sometimes, the Convention doesn\u2019t have time to wait for the Masses to send crude probes, and PDC scientists step in with brute force and mathematics. Void Engineers deploy quantum-entangled virtual particle emitters linked to an AI array that models the target area as it should be: obedient to the Anthropic Principle and the Technocratic laws of physics. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=1499754#post1499754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are. The writers that thought otherwise were very bad at math. Four dice of countermagick at difficulty 8 comes out behind potentially double the dice pool at difficulty 4 (disabling complex electronics makes JT and Gremlins very easy to use). Jam Gun is similarly easy to use to take out their ranged weapons, and is Rank 1, so even more widespread; the CoGs have another variant that has a difficulty if WP (so, 5, for HIT Marks) and takes out all manufactured weapons for the admittedly not too long duration. War Drones empowered by the Weaver are substantially greater direct physical threat, because they can regenerate agg like Garou regenerate lethal, hit hard, and don't look even remotely different from any other human, as opposed to being 300 kg terminators that werebeasts, by dint of their senses, can instantly pick out of a crowd as wrong and dangerous without needing Sense Weaver (not commonly known, because everyone is concentrated on the Wyrm).</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically, nearly every NPC character is shit. But if you really want to bring mechanics to the forefront, all the Werewolf Legends and Elders fall behind Vampire Methuselahs, Elder Mummies, Fae Lord and Master Mages (nevermind Archmages) even though lore wise, they are supposed to be somewhat equal.<br /> <br /> By the way, you are talking about old models. The newest one looks like a buff human at most.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> HIT Mark X \u2013 \u201cThe Invisible Soldier\u201d<br /> Today\u2019s standard HIT Mark model, the Mark X looks like an<br /> ordinary human who\u2019s strong, fast, and extremely deadly, with a<br /> limited face-shifting ability that allows it to make cosmetic changes<br /> to its features, gender, and skin tone. Without internal examination<br /> or magick, a Mark X remains indistinguishable from a muscular, if<br /> somewhat taciturn, human being. Such machines are no better at<br /> social banter than any previous HIT Mark model, but they\u2019re smart<br /> enough to know how to conceal this weakness; given the decline of<br /> social graces in recent years, such concealment isn\u2019t difficult. </div> </div> </div>Really though, your answers baffled me so much that I will not even bother to reply to them again. Especially since I had to do it a second-time thanks to this old forumware.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27335,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","user":"Technoma","date":". 12-15-2022, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T12:06:59-08:00","id":1499773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=1499762#post1499762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't speak nonsense, they are built so that their host survives all but the most horrendous amount of damage and they are built by Prime 5, Life 4, Matter 2. Why would such oxymoronic flaw would exists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they have to be constructed out of something, and that something is often a substance that a B field can pull on. It is, in fact, a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fail-safes_in_nanotechnology#Ferrous_nanoparticles\" target=\"_blank\">listed common nanotech fail-safe</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Uhuh, so give me an actual example of why please. If you want to bring other fictions facts about Nanites, I can do it too and we would go around giving contradictory examples. </div> </div> </div>Prey is written by someone who was an absolute stickler for hard science. Now, you can say that your nanites are made of something else, but that something else only invites both hard science and technobabble counters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you seen The Technocracy? Half the stuff they have aren't based on any known principles and the rest is outright technobabble that might as well be magic. Even at low levels, All Triggers Locked, to the highest, like Format Space. </div> </div> </div>And that's what invites Paradox. So, at a minimum, a completely &quot;magickal&quot; set of nanites would invite Paradox every time someone gets damaged. At that point, it's basically a marathon that anyone can run, because you just have to keep smacking them with rockets and grenades.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mechanically, nearly every NPC character is shit. But if you really want to bring mechanics to the forefront, all the Werewolf Legends and Elders fall behind Vampire Methuselahs, Elder Mummies, Fae Lord and Master Mages (nevermind Archmages) even though lore wise, they are supposed to be somewhat equal. </div> </div> </div>You: We have an army!<br /> Me, Quite Ironically Taking the Place of Tony Stark: We have kaiju. Also in an army.<br /> <br /> Check the Gifts in Apocalypse and the capacity of Mokole in W20 to not have any stated limit on Tall and Huge Size for Archid. Werewolf can easily bump the game into Godzilla and Gamera territory - possibly even the end of The Cloverfield Paradox, if enough characters use Gift of Giants in one scene to keep one-upping each other. That's just some nifty escalation that got tucked into the end of the line because, well, at that point, you're bringing the Apocalypse on your own terms. Also, the systems aren't built very well for it, unless you ignore smaller characters' stats the same way that a human might ignore a mouse or an ant and just have giant-sized characters duking it out normally among themselves.<br /> <br /> Even without that, though, there's always the option to summon paradox-spirits to deal with mages (level two rite, takes time, but can do it). Ananasi have a splat that's so good at it they literally only take about as much time as it does to whistle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the way, you are talking about old models. The newest one looks like a buff human at most. </div> </div> </div>I have seen that stat block in my copy of the M20 pdf, yes. Given the &quot;no better at social banter&quot;, a lupus could probably still pick them out of a crowd at ease due to their lack of appropriate social cues. They're really good at body language, what with relying mostly on non-language cues and all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really though, your answers baffled me so much that I will not even bother to reply to them again. Especially since I had to do it a second-time thanks to this old forumware. </div> </div> </div>That's half outside of my control, and I have to admit, it's really annoying, though I also adapted to cutting my response if I suspected that there would be a time-out and pasting it after logging in again. As for the other half, I'm not sure why they're baffling. The mechanics of dueling Gift vs countermagick don't work out well for the countermagick. In the case of most HIT Marks being targeted by Jam Technology, a conceivable Manipulation + Craft pool of eight dice at difficult 4 (expected value: 4.8) equals more successes than four dice at difficulty 8 (expected value: 0.8), even with doubled successes for magick vs other powers. That's an average of three turns or so, and that's a lot of damage to take without the possibility of defense. Hence, my cavalier attitude toward the TU's rad killer cyborgs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 12-15-2022, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T16:20:58-08:00","id":1499795,"title":"","content":"Regarding Technocracy versus Werewolf, whoever sees and shoots first is probably going to win. Both possess powerful enough alpha-strike capabilities and countermeasures that the side which has the opportunity to prepare said options is going to be the one with an advantage. And in the case of both groups being surprised, it will be a crapshoot depending on the tools each group happens to have in their toolbox without anticipating the situation. I'd be inclined to agree that Jam Technology should work on Technocrat gear, but I'd be surprised if Technocrats built their nanobots to be vulnerable to mundane magnetism.<br /> <br /> Back on topic!<br /> <br /> I feel like the question of whether or not Mages/Technocrats can create some kind of facsimile of a Changing Breed, some kind of shapeshifter based on a particular type of animal with multiple forms and other supernatural advantages or powers, is obviously true. So I think the more interesting question is whether or not they could create a genuine Mockery Breed, an artificially-created Fera that possesses traits like Rage and Gnosis. And whether or not that should be possible is going to depend on a particular question: whether or not the creation of the original Mockery Breeds required the involvement of a high-level spirit like a Maeljin or some other kind of Wyrmish Incarna.<br /> <br /> If Pentex could do it without needing some kind of powerful spirit patron to provide traits like Gnosis for their Mockery Breeds, then I feel like it should be possible for a Mage. If they weren't relying on a powerful Bane, then Pentex probably did use the Technephandi from the Special Projects Division as part of the process. And if they didn't receive help from an Incarna or a Mage, then I'd have a hard time buying the idea that they could do it but a Mage could not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T09:50:08-08:00","id":1499862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=1499795#post1499795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Technocracy versus Werewolf, whoever sees and shoots first is probably going to win. Both possess powerful enough alpha-strike capabilities and countermeasures that the side which has the opportunity to prepare said options is going to be the one with an advantage. And in the case of both groups being surprised, it will be a crapshoot depending on the tools each group happens to have in their toolbox without anticipating the situation. I'd be inclined to agree that Jam Technology should work on Technocrat gear, but I'd be surprised if Technocrats built their nanobots to be vulnerable to mundane magnetism.<br /> <br /> Back on topic!<br /> <br /> I feel like the question of whether or not Mages/Technocrats can create some kind of facsimile of a Changing Breed, some kind of shapeshifter based on a particular type of animal with multiple forms and other supernatural advantages or powers, is obviously true. So I think the more interesting question is whether or not they could create a genuine Mockery Breed, an artificially-created Fera that possesses traits like Rage and Gnosis. And whether or not that should be possible is going to depend on a particular question: whether or not the creation of the original Mockery Breeds required the involvement of a high-level spirit like a Maeljin or some other kind of Wyrmish Incarna.<br /> <br /> If Pentex could do it without needing some kind of powerful spirit patron to provide traits like Gnosis for their Mockery Breeds, then I feel like it should be possible for a Mage. If they weren't relying on a powerful Bane, then Pentex probably did use the Technephandi from the Special Projects Division as part of the process. And if they didn't receive help from an Incarna or a Mage, then I'd have a hard time buying the idea that they could do it but a Mage could not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a better framework for addressing the &quot;But why didn't Mages do it?&quot; would be the Alchemical Demiurge trait from Exalted (specifically, the second edition presentation of Alchemical Exalted). Only mortals can have it, so even Solars that have every Craft, Lore, and Occult Charm and cough out five dot Artifacts can't just make their own Champions willy nilly; in fact, they can't do it at all, because it requires being linked to Autochthon in a way that only mortals without power are, and Solars vastly outstripped that the day they took their Second Breath. The same applies to the other Exalted, no matter how high their crafting-appropriate Traits rise - they have a &quot;set paradigm&quot; that doesn't involve letting another transcendent power take the wheel and drive.<br /> <br /> So, no, Mages aren't necessary, and aren't even necessarily going to be good at it. In fact, they might even disrupt the process and doom the subjects just by being in the near vicinity of the project. Paradox is a hell of a drug, after all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T11:40:33-08:00","id":1499871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/490214-build-yourown-mockery-breed-because-i-m-a-mage-damn-it?p=1499862#post1499862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a better framework for addressing the &quot;But why didn't Mages do it?&quot; would be the Alchemical Demiurge trait from Exalted (specifically, the second edition presentation of Alchemical Exalted). Only mortals can have it, so even Solars that have every Craft, Lore, and Occult Charm and cough out five dot Artifacts can't just make their own Champions willy nilly; in fact, they can't do it at all, because it requires being linked to Autochthon in a way that only mortals without power are, and Solars vastly outstripped that the day they took their Second Breath. The same applies to the other Exalted, no matter how high their crafting-appropriate Traits rise - they have a &quot;set paradigm&quot; that doesn't involve letting another transcendent power take the wheel and drive.<br /> <br /> So, no, Mages aren't necessary, and aren't even necessarily going to be good at it. In fact, they might even disrupt the process and doom the subjects just by being in the near vicinity of the project. Paradox is a hell of a drug, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have very little familiarity with Exalted. But I can see what you're getting at, and it is a point that I hadn't considered. A good World of Darkness parallel would be the fact that, IIRC, a Kinfolk that is born with Gnosis can never Awaken. There may be some kind of fundamental metaphysical incompatibility there that would, ironically, allow the non-Awakened to achieve something that the Awakened can't. After my post, I had been considering that arguably the greatest challenge would be removing things like Paradox or the risk of the entire thing unraveling through Disbelief, which would be necessary for the original Mockery Breeds as well if Mages were involved in their creation.<br /> <br /> That said, I tend to be a fan of the &quot;in theory, Mages can achieve just about anything, it's just a question of how tough the requirements are&quot; approach, so I'm disinclined to take the &quot;completely impossible&quot; perspective, but that's a personal preference rather than a fact. It might be that you'd need something like Archspheres or extremely special circumstances, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}